What changed, what to test
1. Refactored pcb slot. Changed how pcb supported. Now its 1 mm edge around perimeter. for print settings is recommended to reduce XY distance to supports to something like 0.2 so that edge can be supprted properly. Aslo is very benefitial to have interface without gaps so that top part of supports is solid. that greatly improves pcb slot surface quality and make them come off as one piece.
2. Battery cover logic changed. Now its completely unbined from basemesh and instead its positioned realative to middle pcb supports. "battery thickness" parameter defines distance between bottom of middle supports to the battery cover. This is made to avoid dependencies on the basemesh and improve controllability of the battery compartment.
3."No battery" logic removed and changed to separate basemesh. Now you can swap between battery and no battery using checkbox in global parameters. That will just swap between  basemesh GripX and basemesh GripX no battery collection and will remove battery boolean. No battery option  is currently only working for GripX.
3. Vertex groups are no longer required. They are completely removed.
4. Basemesh for GripX is adapted to work in hollow fill mode. Shape is refined to have better topology.
5. Fixed errors in R2R4 geometry logic. Affected parameters are trigger length and shear, so their values might not produce same effect. To match shape is better to import reference stl and double check.
6. Refactored stick logic, parameters and else. Unfortunately it will require manual parameter matching from old parameter nodegroups since names and order of some parameters have changed. Base logic is same, most of changes affect stick top custiomizations. Now topmost offset is universal for all stick top customizations. Refined logic so that its more coherent and stable.
7. Fill logic is refactored and separated between variants. Since logic is greatly affected it will not match to previous parameters and will require tuning. Though i hope its not too critical.
8. Hollow fill is tested, seem working between GripX and GripR1. THough i would prefer to have more tests. Print settings are quire crucial in hollow fill mode. Intricate geometry must be printed as clean as possible, have least amount of wrapping and should stick well to bed for it to assemeble well. Print must be cleaned thoroghly and critical spots must be checked. Middle plate could be tuned in future to potentially provide better clapming force to use without screws. Currently it might not be sufficient for holding controller together without them. Middle plate should be printed with settings oprimized for best support contact quality. Using solid interface greatly impoves that. Bottom case also should use minmal support Z distance since R2R4 are floating above bed, and required to be printed perfectly and stick to top of supoorts well. For bottom hollow case is bettter to use normal or snug supports for that reason, to provide best support for R2R4 shafts. Top hollow case requires to use tree suppports since there are spots above R1L1 that make removing reqular supports impossible.
9. Removed options for unrefined features like phone holder and clip, and button cap for R2R4. Might get back to those later.
10. Refactored DPAD there was some errors and inconsistencies. will probably need to be matched to previous parameters.Refactored button caps, should be more controllable and consistent.
11. All changes are made to provide better contollability and interchangeability between modes. All changes made can be reversed and branched if outcome is not satisfactory. We can bracnh parameters for hollow fill and regular mode. If shape is not drastically worse is better to avoid branching but if change is too drastic and hurt ergonomics we can branch without problems.
12. Slightly adjusted R1L1 parameters for hollow fill mode. Original parameters are stored in same nodegroup.
13. Got back the pillars. it seem like pcb slot geometry is slightly misalined so if theres no pillars whole pcb was shifted in Y slightly. That what was probably causing stick misalingment. Will correct pcb slot shape so that it centers pcb even without pillars. But anyways is good to have them as an option.
14. Changed reinforcers so that they also reinforce nut pocket from all sides. Theres high chance of nut twisting and bending pla during installation, so adding some reinforcement around might reduce that.
